      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): handle stderr stream errors in tool_search_code child",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`tool_search_code` spawns a Node child and reads stderr. If the stderr stream emits an error event, it is not handled and can become an unhandled exception.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd an explicit `child.stderr?.on(\"error\", ...)` listener that rejects the run promise, mirroring the existing `child.on(\"error\")` handling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTool Search code-mode runs are more resilient to transient stream failures.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added regression test in `src/agents/tool-search.stream-errors.test.ts`.\n- Exposed `runCodeModeChild` and `ToolSearchRuntime` on the `testing` barrel for focused testing.\n- Added real behavior proof at `scripts/proof/tool-search-code-mode-stream-errors.mts`.\n- Local run:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tool-search.stream-errors.test.ts` passed\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/tool-search.ts src/agents/tool-search.stream-errors.test.ts scripts/proof/tool-search-code-mode-stream-errors.mts` passed\n",
        "branch": "fix/tool-search-code-mode-stream-errors",
        "head_sha": "e5bd55e3c68ceb562c7acacfb9d5da719d148f24",
